---
import "../../styles/animations.css";
---

<figure class="an-wrap">
  <svg class="an ch" viewBox="0 0 480 242" role="img" aria-label="A consumer reads new log entries from its cursor"><rect class="nd " x="16" y="16" width="448" height="84" rx="12"/><image href="/images/ruvio-mark-128.png" x="26" y="25" width="22" height="22"/><text class="b" x="251.0" y="41" text-anchor="middle">Shard write log</text><g class="ch-w5"><rect x="34" y="56" width="62" height="34" rx="6" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--grid)"/><text class="sm m" x="65" y="78" text-anchor="middle">#1</text></g><g class="ch-w6"><rect x="106" y="56" width="62" height="34" rx="6" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--grid)"/><text class="sm m" x="137" y="78" text-anchor="middle">#2</text></g><g class="ch-w7"><rect x="178" y="56" width="62" height="34" rx="6" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--grid)"/><text class="sm m" x="209" y="78" text-anchor="middle">#3</text></g><g class="ch-w8"><rect x="250" y="56" width="62" height="34" rx="6" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--grid)"/><text class="sm m" x="281" y="78" text-anchor="middle">#4</text></g><g class="ch-w9"><rect x="322" y="56" width="62" height="34" rx="6" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--grid)"/><text class="sm m" x="353" y="78" text-anchor="middle">#5</text></g><g class="ch-w10"><rect x="394" y="56" width="62" height="34" rx="6" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--grid)"/><text class="sm m" x="425" y="78" text-anchor="middle">#6</text></g><g class="ch-w3"><rect x="175" y="53" width="146" height="40" rx="8" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2"/></g><g class="ch-w4"><rect x="319" y="53" width="146" height="40" rx="8" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2"/></g><rect class="nd " x="150" y="126" width="180" height="52" rx="12"/><text class="b" x="251.0" y="151" text-anchor="middle">Consumer</text><g class="ch-w0"><text class="sm m" x="256" y="168" text-anchor="middle">cursor 2</text></g><g class="ch-w1"><text class="sm m" x="256" y="168" text-anchor="middle">cursor 4</text></g><g class="ch-w2"><text class="sm m" x="256" y="168" text-anchor="middle">cursor 6</text></g><g class="ch-w3"><circle class="pk" cx="256" cy="126" r="5" fill="var(--c1)" style="--dx:0px;--dy:-30px;animation-delay:0s;animation-duration:1.0s!important;"/></g><g class="ch-w4"><circle class="pk" cx="256" cy="126" r="5" fill="var(--c1)" style="--dx:0px;--dy:-30px;animation-delay:0s;animation-duration:1.0s!important;"/></g><rect class="cap" x="16" y="200" width="448" height="38" rx="10"/><g class="ch-w0"><text x="240.0" y="224" text-anchor="middle">Writes append to the shard log.</text></g><g class="ch-w1"><text x="240.0" y="224" text-anchor="middle">The consumer reads from its cursor: only new entries.</text></g><g class="ch-w2 an-fin"><text x="240.0" y="224" text-anchor="middle" style="fill:var(--ok)">No key polling. After a restart it resumes from the cursor.</text></g></svg>
  <figcaption><b>A change feed from a cursor</b>CHANGES returns the writes on a shard after a cursor, so consumers never poll keys.</figcaption>
</figure>
